$DIR/main.p:1:1: this program starts puroutines, uses channels or waits in pluto/sync, so it needs a scheduler, and none is bound: mark a package-level variable whose type implements rt.Scheduler with //pu:scheduler (language spec section 4.7; hosted builds bind one by default)
    This program starts puroutines, uses channels or waits in pluto/sync, so it
    needs a scheduler, and none is bound. Hosted builds bind one by default; a
    freestanding program, such as a kernel, provides its own: a package-level
    variable marked //pu:scheduler whose type implements rt.Scheduler.
    Plutonium carries a scheduler only in programs that ask for one, and a
    kernel supplies its own, so a freestanding program must say which.
    Bind the kernel's scheduler:
        //pu:scheduler
        var scheduler kernelScheduler
    (see "go starts a puroutine" in the Plutonium spec, section 4.7)
    (run "pluto explain E2583" for a longer explanation)
